<span class="tok-comment"># 4. Fixed static resolution and channel count in HWC (or Image[3, 1080, 1920] for CHW)</span>
<span class="tok-keyword">accept</span> <span class="tok-type">Image[1080, 1920, 3]</span> <span class="tok-var">$frame</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="doc-p">
            <strong>How Image Works with each (Channel Slicing):</strong>
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-list" style="margin: 0 0 16px 20px; color: var(--grey-800); line-height: 1.65;">
            <li><strong>Iteration Axis:</strong> Crucially, each on an Image slices along the <strong>Color Channel Axis</strong> (C), <em>not</em> spatial rows or columns!
              <br />• In hwc layout: slices along <strong>Axis 2</strong>.
              <br />• In chw layout: slices along <strong>Axis 0</strong>.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Iteration Count:</strong> Exactly C parallel workers (e.g. 3 for RGB, 4 for RGBA).</li>
            <li><strong>Loop Variable Derivation:</strong> Each parallel iteration receives an independent rank-2 <strong>Image</strong> in ColorSpace::Grayscale, preserving the full H &times; W spatial resolution. This allows applying filters, equalizations, or thresholding to individual channels simultaneously.</li>
            <li><strong>Payload Kind Preservation (E009):</strong> The sub-flow inside each must preserve the payload kind. You cannot convert the channel slice into a Tensor or Audio mid-loop without causing static error E009.</li>
            <li><strong>Restacking:</strong> The transformed grayscale channel slices are reassembled along the channel axis back into the parent's original color space and layout. Because the slices are recombined into the higher-rank Image, all iterations must produce compatible single-channel Image payloads.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

